WEBVTT

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:18.530
Yaichiro was captured by the Friday Fellows.

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:23.120
Kinkaku said on the phone earlier that he 
and Ginkaku are teaching Yasaburo a lesson…

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:26.870
Your mom got caught too, but 
I don't know where she is.

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:43.100
We can just leave him be.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.520
He can't do anything.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:32.000
<b>Episode 12: 
The False Eizan Electric Railway</b>

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:38.770
Big Brother!

00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:43.290
Whoa, whoa, Yashiro. 
What are you doing here?

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:47.680
Raijin is on a rampage. 
Why aren't you with Mother?

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:49.300
Big Brother,

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:52.750
everyone's been captured by the Ebisugawas!

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:54.350
What the heck?!

00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:57.140
You're the only one we can count on!

00:02:57.140 --> 00:03:02.000
But you know, I'm a frog in a well.

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.700
What are you saying I can do about it?

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:07.740
I have an idea!

00:03:08.110 --> 00:03:10.830
Turn this way and open your mouth.

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:12.290
Sheesh,

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:16.090
I don't think this is the time to 
take it easy drinking rainwater.

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:17.630
Just open up!

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:49.540
Big Brother?

00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:52.070
Big Brother!

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:56.670
I'm back in the game!

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:03.380
<b>Chikurintei Soba</b>

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:08.970
Your older brother was a good 
tanuki. It's such a shame.

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:10.370
Bullshit!

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:12.530
It's not bullshit.

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:15.930
Certainly I'll never forget the 
pain in my butt when he bit it.

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:19.860
It almost got an extra crack!

00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:23.460
But it's true that he was an earnest tanuki.

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:25.110
So save him!

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:29.760
No can do. We gotta obey 
our father, you know.

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:31.960
This tanuki business is rough.

00:04:39.010 --> 00:04:42.050
What's going on, Ginkaku? 
Why are we shaking so much?

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:43.810
I dunno, Big Brother.

00:04:43.810 --> 00:04:47.120
It feels like I'm going 
really fast... somehow!

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:50.250
I'm so scared my butt is twitching!

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:53.020
Calm down, Ginkaku! You're 
gonna lose your transformation!

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:55.890
But I'm scared, I can't hold it anymore!

00:04:56.110 --> 00:04:57.690
No!

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:03.820
I said, noooo!

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:17.930
What happened?

00:05:17.930 --> 00:05:19.880
Big Brother, uh, we're moving.

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:28.610
Big Brother, we came to save you.

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:30.080
Yashiro!

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:32.440
What in the world...?

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:36.850
Yasaburo! How's my driving?

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:39.020
Yajiro!

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:51.710
You jerks did sure did a number on me before!

00:05:53.170 --> 00:05:54.670
Quit it, you pervert!

00:05:54.670 --> 00:05:57.160
<i>Don't</i> take off our underwear!

00:05:57.160 --> 00:05:59.740
You're gonna regret this, for real!

00:05:59.740 --> 00:06:01.780
Stop!

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:07.940
Well this is cozy.

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:10.260
Yasaburo! Don't be so rough!

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:12.460
I'm the one who should be saying that!

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:17.230
The Fujin Raijin folding fan!

00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:19.130
So you had it!

00:06:20.340 --> 00:06:22.980
We found it by Aoi Bridge. 
We didn't steal it!

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:24.450
Shush!

00:06:25.010 --> 00:06:29.240
This is Prof. Akadama's 
fan, so I'm returning it.

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:39.420
Make way! Make way! The Ei 
Train is comin' through!

00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:49.680
Aiiee, what should I do, Yasaburo?!

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:54.790
The head of our family, our 
brother, is in a helluva pinch,

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:58.460
but somehow I'm having a bizarre 
amount of fun. I can't help it!

00:06:58.460 --> 00:07:00.350
How ridiculous!

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:02.580
Who cares? Don't stop, Big Brother!

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:05.680
This is another manifestation 
of our idiot blood.

00:07:06.030 --> 00:07:08.650
What is fun is good!

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:20.250
What is fun is good!

00:07:26.110 --> 00:07:28.960
What's up? Are you okay?

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:32.540
Those were Father's last words.

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:36.810
He said that to me that night.

00:07:37.340 --> 00:07:42.230
I couldn't think of it all that 
time at the bottom of the well,

00:07:42.880 --> 00:07:45.770
but finally, just now, I remembered.

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:53.030
What is fun is good!

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:01.450
You're gonna keep going this way?

00:08:01.450 --> 00:08:03.680
What'd you say? I can't hear you!

00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:06.510
Pontocho! We're going to Pontocho!

00:08:06.510 --> 00:08:09.050
I wonder where Pontocho is...

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:15.090
Can you turn left on Sanjo?

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:17.280
Not a chance.

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:31.820
Okay, that was kinda bad.

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:36.630
Wouldn't it be better to stop 
the train and run on foot?

00:08:36.630 --> 00:08:40.590
Sorry Yasaburo, doesn't seem 
like it's gonna happen.

00:08:40.590 --> 00:08:43.870
Well, there's no helping it. Let's 
take Shijo Street for a bit.

00:09:09.890 --> 00:09:14.220
Big Brother, we're running past 
the same place over and over.

00:09:17.650 --> 00:09:21.850
This is messed up. Let's slow down a bit!

00:09:21.850 --> 00:09:27.250
Yasaburo, you make some 
pretty delicate requests...

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:29.900
I'm working on it, but...

00:09:29.900 --> 00:09:33.670
The idiot blood seething 
within you won't be calmed?

00:09:34.060 --> 00:09:35.970
Doesn't seem like it.

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:50.920
This is a False Teramachi Street!

00:09:53.410 --> 00:09:54.420
You!

00:09:54.420 --> 00:09:56.300
My cell phone!

00:09:56.300 --> 00:09:58.010
Whadaya think, Yasaburo?

00:09:58.010 --> 00:10:01.380
"It's just one thing after 
another," for you, huh.

00:10:01.380 --> 00:10:04.970
I called the Ebisugawa Elite Guard 
and had them go ahead of us.

00:10:04.970 --> 00:10:06.160
Had them go ahead of us!

00:10:06.380 --> 00:10:10.050
How many traps do you have to 
plant before you guys are happy?!

00:10:10.050 --> 00:10:11.430
Are you sorry now?

00:10:11.430 --> 00:10:12.840
Are ya?

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:15.550
You're going straight into the Kamo River!

00:10:16.310 --> 00:10:17.950
Big Brother, we're screwed.

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:19.220
Mm, screwed.

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:30.400
My cell phone!

00:10:35.210 --> 00:10:38.660
At this rate we're gonna end 
up diving right into the river!

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:43.010
The Kamo River's cold in 
winter! Better limber up!

00:10:43.010 --> 00:10:45.250
Yay, we tricked you!

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:47.620
Back in the game, back in the game!

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:51.430
Hey, you guys are falling into 
the river, too, you know!

00:10:52.030 --> 00:10:54.340
You mean, we "share the same fate."

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:57.180
Enemies in the same boat, 
enemies in the same boat!

00:10:57.970 --> 00:10:59.760
Yashiro, brace yourself!

00:11:08.980 --> 00:11:11.980
<b>Chitose-ya</b>

00:11:08.980 --> 00:11:11.980
<b>Minamiza</b>

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:23.380
We tricked'em! We tricked'em!

00:11:23.380 --> 00:11:25.990
The ones who got tricked were you guys!

00:11:33.660 --> 00:11:37.340
The Flying Eizan Electric 
Railway! And a fake, at that!

00:11:48.150 --> 00:11:50.920
So we didn't have to take 
a cold dip after all.

00:11:51.780 --> 00:11:52.940
Victory!

00:11:58.210 --> 00:11:59.580
There they are!

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:01.770
Crap.

00:12:01.770 --> 00:12:04.720
We... we tricked you, Yasaburo!

00:12:06.020 --> 00:12:10.850
Big Brother? What are you saying? We don't--

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:16.550
W-Well, actually I thought 
this might happen and...

00:12:16.550 --> 00:12:19.940
there's actually a gigantic maneki-neko 
in the Kamo River, which is really--

00:12:19.940 --> 00:12:21.130
W-W-Wait a sec!

00:12:21.130 --> 00:12:23.990
Let us take a quick break, 
just a little break!

00:12:23.990 --> 00:12:26.960
I can't wait, because there's no time.

00:12:26.960 --> 00:12:29.140
Hope you get carried all 
the way to Osaka Bay.

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:33.500
I don't wanna get thrown in the water again!

00:12:33.750 --> 00:12:35.650
It's cold, we'll die! For serious!

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:37.830
Hey, you guys,

00:12:38.070 --> 00:12:42.090
the Friday Fellows are having their 
year-end bash just over there!

00:12:42.090 --> 00:12:47.030
Do you prefer the cold Kamo 
River, or the hot iron po--

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:57.990
Flying through the sky sure is wacky.

00:12:58.390 --> 00:13:01.720
Big Brother, over there 
are the Friday Fellows!

00:13:01.720 --> 00:13:04.100
Please pull up to the 
back of that restaurant.

00:13:04.100 --> 00:13:07.350
You make some difficult requests...

00:13:07.350 --> 00:13:10.560
This is my first time, remember.

00:13:11.110 --> 00:13:15.310
I'll try getting a little wind up 
with the Fujin Raijin folding fan.

00:13:22.680 --> 00:13:24.860
Be careful.

00:13:25.310 --> 00:13:27.610
Easy does it, easy does it.

00:13:40.600 --> 00:13:42.550
Ow, my nose.

00:14:01.050 --> 00:14:02.350
Yashiro!

00:14:02.350 --> 00:14:07.170
Run straight to Sensuiro and 
disrupt the elders' discussion!

00:14:07.600 --> 00:14:08.710
Okay!

00:14:09.070 --> 00:14:10.720
Delay them as much as you can.

00:14:10.720 --> 00:14:14.800
If it doesn't seem to be going 
well, fan the room a little bit.

00:14:15.350 --> 00:14:17.500
Once you're done with that, give 
the fan back to Prof. Akadama.

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:20.300
He should be at Sensuiro, too.

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:22.050
What about you?

00:14:22.050 --> 00:14:24.920
I'll follow after rescuing 
our brother here. Get going!

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:27.950
If you stick around looking 
like that, you'll get eaten!

00:14:31.330 --> 00:14:32.970
Yasaburo?

00:14:40.540 --> 00:14:43.390
Dammit, dammit!

00:14:43.390 --> 00:14:46.320
You probably think I'm a fool,

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:50.450
imitating humans, shouting about 
elections and groundwork-laying...

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:53.030
After all that, this is how I end up!

00:14:53.030 --> 00:14:57.610
A tanuki this pathetic can't shoulder 
the future of tanuki society!

00:14:57.930 --> 00:15:00.860
I wish I would have just been eaten!

00:15:00.860 --> 00:15:03.720
That's way overkill.

00:15:03.720 --> 00:15:06.000
Trying to make Mother cry again?

00:15:06.910 --> 00:15:10.180
But what a failure of a tanuki I am.

00:15:11.120 --> 00:15:14.640
It's just a manifestation of our idiot blood.

00:15:15.450 --> 00:15:18.290
And imitating humans, nothing 
wrong with that, is there?

00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:21.260
You're following in 
Father's footsteps, right?

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:23.270
I guess...

00:15:23.610 --> 00:15:25.610
Crush Ebisugawa!

00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:28.180
We gotta take revenge for Father!

00:15:28.180 --> 00:15:29.480
What?

00:15:29.480 --> 00:15:33.430
The one who handed him over to 
the Friday Fellows was Soun.

00:15:35.190 --> 00:15:37.220
It's me, Big Brother.

00:15:37.220 --> 00:15:38.850
Yajiro?

00:15:38.850 --> 00:15:40.810
Hurry up, let's go!

00:15:40.810 --> 00:15:44.130
I sent Yashiro ahead to Sensuiro, 
so we can still make it on time.

00:15:44.850 --> 00:15:46.770
Mother will be happy this way, too.

00:15:46.770 --> 00:15:48.630
Oh, right, Mother!

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:51.890
Did you save her? Did you?

00:15:51.890 --> 00:15:54.860
Well, not yet. I don't know where she is.

00:15:54.860 --> 00:15:57.890
She's at the Electric Brandy 
shop at Kamiya Bridge.

00:15:57.890 --> 00:15:59.450
We gotta rescue her--

00:15:59.450 --> 00:16:02.230
Calm down! I'll go.

00:16:06.950 --> 00:16:08.860
Who's there?

00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:17.850
Run! Leave Mother to me!

00:16:29.210 --> 00:16:32.350
Oh my, that's quite a predicament.

00:16:33.060 --> 00:16:34.760
Who might you be?

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:38.920
I heard a big noise and was like, 
"Huh, I wonder what that was."

00:16:38.920 --> 00:16:41.710
Just passing by, then?

00:16:51.040 --> 00:16:52.670
You know him?

00:16:52.910 --> 00:16:55.210
Yes, Jurojin.

00:16:55.600 --> 00:16:58.020
He's a really fun guy.

00:16:58.020 --> 00:17:02.120
Is that so? Fun is good.

00:17:02.520 --> 00:17:06.830
Hoo boy, I wonder what happened.

00:17:06.830 --> 00:17:10.360
Must have been an earthquake. 
Or maybe a tornado?

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:14.880
My tanuki ran away!

00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:17.950
Hey you, what the heck happened?

00:17:17.950 --> 00:17:21.830
Some terrifyingly large object came crashing 
in from the direction of the Kamo River--

00:17:21.830 --> 00:17:24.180
I dunno what's going on anymore!

00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:28.150
Look, the room is a mess, the tanuki's gone.

00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:31.150
Well, calm down, Hotei.

00:17:31.150 --> 00:17:36.360
But I worked so hard to 
finally get that tanuki!

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:42.360
It's no use going off about 
all that at some passerby.

00:17:43.300 --> 00:17:48.160
Sometimes in this city things happen

00:17:48.160 --> 00:17:50.940
that we can't explain.

00:17:50.940 --> 00:17:54.760
There's no need to get upset and 
shorten your lifespan over each one.

00:17:56.000 --> 00:17:57.630
Don't worry!

00:17:57.630 --> 00:18:03.200
When I stopped by the Electric Brandy 
shop at Kamiya Bridge earlier

00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:05.870
I saw a tanuki.

00:18:05.870 --> 00:18:09.110
Apparently my acquaintance was keeping it,

00:18:09.110 --> 00:18:12.620
but I already asked him about what 
we could do in a case like this.

00:18:12.620 --> 00:18:16.340
Let's just boil that one in 
our hot pot this evening.

00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:24.620
Good grief, we're off to a bad 
start. We'll have to go elsewhere.

00:18:25.160 --> 00:18:26.720
I wonder where would be good.

00:18:26.720 --> 00:18:30.270
Oh? Do we finally get to see 
that private train of yours?

00:18:30.270 --> 00:18:34.910
Unfortunately, it's in the shop.

00:18:34.910 --> 00:18:37.030
I'm not sure if you can 
call it a replacement,

00:18:37.030 --> 00:18:41.130
but there's this restaurant with a 
pretty nice atmosphere, Sensuiro.

00:18:41.130 --> 00:18:45.930
I thought something like this might happen, 
so I made a reservation just in case.

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:47.680
H-H-Hold on!

00:18:47.680 --> 00:18:50.880
Would it be all right if I accompanied you?

00:18:50.880 --> 00:18:52.610
Hmm? You?

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:56.600
I've always wanted to try eating tanuki,

00:18:56.600 --> 00:19:00.480
and before we eat I'd really like 
to meet it living and breathing!

00:19:00.480 --> 00:19:04.120
I've never seen a real live tanuki before!

00:19:06.850 --> 00:19:11.390
I don't have an issue with it, so...?

00:19:11.390 --> 00:19:14.830
If Benten is okay with it, 
then it's okay with me.

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:19.580
Sorry, but since you're young, I'd 
like to ask some grunt work of you.

00:19:19.830 --> 00:19:23.330
There is some Electric Brandy in the kitchen.

00:19:23.330 --> 00:19:26.930
Take it to Sensuiro.

00:19:26.930 --> 00:19:28.980
Understood!

00:19:34.440 --> 00:19:38.010
Yaichiro lost his nerve and ran away.

00:19:38.010 --> 00:19:41.770
We can just forget about that coward.

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:46.980
Well, there's nothing we 
can do if he's not here.

00:20:01.520 --> 00:20:03.260
What a racket!

00:20:05.220 --> 00:20:09.270
What do you think you're doing, 
ignoring me and screwing around?

00:20:09.490 --> 00:20:13.220
P-Please accept our humble apologies.

00:20:13.220 --> 00:20:16.860
It's just that a whirlwind 
suddenly whipped through...

00:20:16.860 --> 00:20:19.850
Could it be that you caused--

00:20:19.850 --> 00:20:22.040
What are you talking about?!

00:20:22.040 --> 00:20:25.200
Who do you think I am?

00:20:26.530 --> 00:20:30.870
I came all the way here in the first place

00:20:27.530 --> 00:20:29.040
Nice job.

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:34.250
because you hairballs asked me to!

00:20:32.110 --> 00:20:33.970
Guess I'll head in.

00:20:34.250 --> 00:20:38.290
Give the folding fan back to 
the professor and lie low. {TB: The most direct translatin is "withdraw" like "stay out of the way" but it's not entirely clear where he's telling him to go. Went with "lie low" cuz no matter where we see him next it won't be weird.}

00:20:48.260 --> 00:20:51.920
My humblest apologies 
for keeping you waiting.

00:20:51.920 --> 00:20:55.010
However, please allow me to explain 
the extenuating circumstances.

00:20:55.010 --> 00:20:59.270
I was held captive by the Friday 
Fellows until just a bit ago.

00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:07.210
Why was I able to be taken by 
the Friday Fellows unaware?

00:21:07.210 --> 00:21:12.000
It was all the plot of Ebisugawa 
Soun, sitting over there.

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:14.710
In order to take the position 
of Nise-emon by force,

00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:18.830
Soun captured all the members of 
the Shimogamo family, including myself.

00:21:18.830 --> 00:21:22.900
He packed me into a cage and handed 
me over to the Friday Fellows.

00:21:22.900 --> 00:21:26.620
This is not at all how a tanuki should act.

00:21:26.620 --> 00:21:28.650
Is that true?

00:21:28.650 --> 00:21:30.350
It is a lie.

00:21:30.600 --> 00:21:35.410
A tanuki who boils tanuki in a hot pot? 
We're not talking about tengu or humans here.

00:21:35.410 --> 00:21:38.970
Such a cruel tanuki does 
not exist in this world.

00:21:38.970 --> 00:21:42.020
He's just trying to cause trouble for me

00:21:42.020 --> 00:21:44.970
as he makes excuses for arriving 
late to this sacred meeting.

00:21:44.970 --> 00:21:47.310
It's an absolutely underhanded 
way to go about things.

00:21:47.310 --> 00:21:50.210
It's baseless slander.

00:21:50.210 --> 00:21:51.620
It is not a lie!

00:21:51.620 --> 00:21:53.810
Where's your proof?

00:21:54.800 --> 00:21:57.330
This is the truth!

00:21:57.330 --> 00:22:01.380
Augh, what a mess this has been.

00:22:02.340 --> 00:22:06.180
Well, well, if it isn't Shimogamo Yajiro!

00:22:06.180 --> 00:22:08.840
Haven't seen you in quite some time!

00:22:08.840 --> 00:22:13.260
We can't consult him! He's a member 
of the Shimogamo family, too!

00:22:13.260 --> 00:22:17.490
They worked out their story 
in a scheme to take me down!

00:22:17.490 --> 00:22:19.420
It doesn't make sense in the first place!

00:22:19.700 --> 00:22:22.920
You say I handed you over 
to the Friday Fellows,

00:22:22.920 --> 00:22:25.670
but then why are you here?

00:22:25.670 --> 00:22:27.870
You don't seem to have 
been boiled in a hot pot!

00:22:28.500 --> 00:22:30.620
It appears some people have 
entered the room next door.

00:22:44.550 --> 00:22:48.630
Tanuki are peace-loving creatures.

00:22:50.060 --> 00:22:53.140
But what is peace in tanuki society?

00:22:54.050 --> 00:22:57.570
If it's lying on the bank of the Kamo River

00:22:57.570 --> 00:23:01.850
and absentmindedly gazing at 
a blue sky, it's attainable.

00:23:02.560 --> 00:23:05.120
It should be easily within our reach.

00:23:06.430 --> 00:23:08.170
So,

00:23:08.500 --> 00:23:12.580
what is this messed up situation we're in?

00:23:15.250 --> 00:23:18.420
You might call it a manifestation 
of our idiot blood,

00:23:19.160 --> 00:23:22.720
but as tanuki, is this really what we want?

00:23:19.160 --> 00:23:26.800
<b>Sensuiro</b>

00:23:30.650 --> 00:23:33.850
Tanuki, humans, and tengu!

00:23:34.060 --> 00:23:36.790
Will there be a happy ending?

00:23:36.790 --> 00:23:39.930
What is fun is good!

00:23:37.520 --> 00:23:39.970
<b>The Eccentric Family</b>
